# .dockerignore — keep secrets, the client bundle, and the workspace out of the image.
#
# ★ `.env` IS THE POINT.
#
# `gate:secrets` scans the repo and `dist/`, and it fails the build when a
# credential appears in a client artifact. It does not scan a Docker image, so
# this file is what stops `.env` being baked into a layer. An image is a file
# someone can pull and inspect — a credential inside one is published, not
# stored. A leaked service-role key bypasses every RLS policy.
#
# The runtime reads its configuration from the environment the platform injects,
# never from a file on disk.

# --- Secrets and local state ------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.supabase-version
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore
*.jks

# --- Not needed by the backend ---------------------------------------------
# The web export is built on the developer's machine and served separately.
dist/
web/
assets/
docs/

# --- Mobile client ----------------------------------------------------------
# The APK is ~95 MB and irrelevant to the server.
app/
android/
ios/
.expo/

# --- Dependencies and caches ------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.worktrees/
.expo-shared/

# --- Version control and tooling -------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.mimocode/
.agents/
.claude/

# --- Tests, evidence, and CI ------------------------------------------------
tests/
docs/
coverage/

# --- Editor and OS noise ----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
